<rml>
<head>
	<title>Doppelganger frame (CDoppelGangerFrame)</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="doppelganger_frame.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="doppelganger_frame">
	<!-- The Doppelganger event HUD (CDoppelGangerFrame): the frame, the monsters that passed, "Time
	     left", the time, the monsters' progress gauge (yellow, orange, red by how many passed), the Ice
	     Walker's marker and the party members' markers on the path. Its workspace slot places #panel
	     at the bottom HUD's scale. Text does not scale: each line takes its native size and cancels the scale. In the
	     background context, behind its other documents (the original drew it under every panel). Takes
	     no pointer events. -->
	<div class="screen">
		<div id="panel">
			<div id="back"></div>
			<!-- The three lines, each placed and coloured by the theme; the monsters-passed line
			     says how many got through. -->
			<span class="frame-text counter-scaled" id="dg_passed" data-class-passed-one="passed_state == 'one'"
			      data-class-passed-several="passed_state == 'several'"
			      data-style-font-size="passed_line.text_px + 'px'">{{passed_line.text}}</span>
			<span class="frame-text counter-scaled" id="dg_time_label" data-style-font-size="time_label.text_px + 'px'">{{time_label.text}}</span>
			<span class="frame-text big counter-scaled" id="dg_time" data-style-font-size="time_line.text_px + 'px'">{{time_line.text}}</span>
			<img class="bar" data-for="b : bars" data-attr-src="b.src" data-attr-rect="b.rect"
			     data-style-left="b.left + 'px'" data-style-width="b.width + 'px'"/>
			<img id="icewalker" src="../../../Double_Micon01.tga" data-if="ice_walker_visible"
			     data-style-left="ice_walker_left + 'px'"/>
			<div class="marker" data-for="m : markers" data-class-hero="m.hero" data-style-left="m.left + 'px'"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
